 "exact_mirror_check": "reconverting with only the affine Y row changed gives new = old mirrored (atlas Z' = -8.6365 - Z) to 2.5e-6 mm, faces identical, for ct_vhm_pfloor (29,816 verts) and ct_vhm_pfloor_fix (7,585); the pre-fix meshes reconvert byte-identically from the committed volume (smooth 1.0 / 0.0).",
 "why_not_a_clean_flip": {
  "rule_frame": "the builder's rules were ported from the female frame where +row = POSTERIOR; in his legs frame +row = ANTERIOR. dy = row - anal_row (line ~573), so every AP rule selects the opposite side",
  "affected_rules": {
   "coccygeus": "dy >= +8 mm 'posterior of the anal centre' -> actually 8+ mm ANTERIOR; after the affine fix its centroid sits 39-41 mm anterior of the anal end, 0.1-1.4 mm from the prostate and 55-63 mm from the coccyx",
   "posterior_pad": "pad = dilation(hull) & (yy > arow): the 14 mm 'posterior' pad is added anteriorly",
   "ischial_spine_level": "anchors(): post = rr > arow - 6 takes the ANTERIOR hip label; k_spine = 752 as built; with the posterior half it is 738 (the lower bound of its search window, i.e. not a clean minimum) -- the pelvic band's top level changes",
   "perineal": "ischiocavernosus (dy <= -12), bulbospongiosus (dy <= -18), deep transverse perineal (dy -40..-8), superficial transverse perineal (dy -28..-12) are all on the wrong side of the anal centre; after the affine fix deep_transverse_perineal_l/r sit 9 mm POSTERIOR of the anal end (should be anterior, urogenital triangle)",
   "not_affected": "external_anal_sphincter ring rule and obturator internus band are AP-symmetric; levator ani = viscera-reach funnel minus the (mis-sided) coccygeus region"
  },
  "needs": "re-running scripts/cryo/vhm_pelvic_floor_from_cryo.py with the affine fix AND the AP rules sign-corrected for the legs frame; that needs his legs cryo frame (SCRATCH/vh_cryo/cryo_legs_frame_{rgb,cls}.npy) and SCRATCH/vhm_ts/legs_total.nii.gz, both absent in this container (resample_cryo_to_ct_frame.py 'legs' branch + a cryo re-stream)"
 },
 "other_observations": {
  "in_plane_stage2_offset": "the pfloor frame carries the legs->torso z offset (-693) but not its in-plane part (+2.72, -0.89 mm) that Q170's viscera use; with it the EAS-to-rectum-cap horizontal offset would drop from 5.9 to ~3.0 mm. Not applied.",
  "winding": "with the corrected (det -1) affine, convert produces inward-wound triangles (signed volume negative), same as ct_vhm_foot/vhm_both; viewer uses DoubleSide + computeVertexNormals, so no visible effect.",
  "vhm_both_vs_ct": "vhm_both coccyx tip is at atlas Y -5.8 while legs_total's sacrum label ends at Y -17.8: his photographic bones and the CT-derived subjects may differ by ~10 mm+ in the coccygeal region (not investigated)"
 },
 "trial_patch": "scratchpad q171/q171_builder_affine_patch.diff (volume_affine() + --reaffine mode); affine-fixed outputs kept in q171/affine_fixed_not_shipped/ -- NOT applied to the repo."
